# CSL - Cursor Desktop Sync

## Rule

Whenever a new `.mdc` rule file is created in `.cursor/rules/` or a new `.plan.md` plan file is created in `.cursor/plans/`, it **must also be copied** to the corresponding folder on the Desktop:

| Source | Desktop Mirror |
|---|---|
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | `/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Rules/` |
| `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` | `/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Plans/` |
| `AGENTS.md` | `/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/AGENTS.md` |
| `.cursorrules` | `/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/cursorrules.txt` |

## When to Sync

1. **After creating a new rule** — copy the `.mdc` file to `~/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Rules/`
2. **After creating a new plan** — copy the `.plan.md` file to `~/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Plans/`
3. **After updating an existing rule or plan** — copy the updated file to overwrite the old version
4. **After updating `AGENTS.md` or `.cursorrules`** — copy to the top-level Desktop folder

## Sync Command

```bash
# Single rule file
cp .cursor/rules/<filename>.mdc "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Rules/"

# Single plan file
cp .cursor/plans/<filename>.plan.md "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Plans/"

# Full re-sync (if needed)
cp .cursor/rules/*.mdc "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Rules/"
cp .cursor/plans/*.plan.md "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/Plans/"
cp AGENTS.md "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/AGENTS.md"
cp .cursorrules "/Users/nathannevedal/Desktop/CSL - Cursor/cursorrules.txt"
```

## Why

The `CSL - Cursor` Desktop folder gives Dr. Nevedal a browsable, Finder-accessible view of all Cursor rules and plans without needing to navigate hidden `.cursor/` directories. It must stay in sync with the workspace originals.